WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.880
- Transformation videos are
all the rage on YouTube.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.560
And recently, Mrwhosetheboss,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.990
did a hundred day body transformation.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.520
Let's see which one of these methods

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.163
is scientifically proven
and which ones are not.

00:00:12.365 --> 00:00:13.860
- A hundred days ago, I challenged myself

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.300
to a fitness a transformation.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.340
This was me, every day I was sleeping

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.660
just four hours a night,

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.430
walking an average of just 2000 steps,

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.440
drinking four cups of caffeinated tea.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.960
- Okay, so there's a lot
happening right off the outset.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.640
What's my feelings on transformations?

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.540
I think they're great,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.130
as long as you're doing them

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.440
with the mindset that you're transforming

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.330
to create a healthy lifestyle.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.960
Otherwise, you're gonna find
yourself in this yo-yo dieting,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.540
crash dieting phase, losing
weight, gaining weight,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.530
losing weight, gaining weight,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.130
and that's problematic because
fat almost has like a memory.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:47.250
So once you have it, it
comes back very quickly.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.230
Sleep four hours a night is terrible.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.880
You're gonna suffer the effects of that

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.290
just several days in.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.240
And I'm talking about shot productivity,

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.910
creativity, metabolism, energy levels,

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.560
everything's gonna struggle there.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.200
Steps, it depends what else
you're doing for exercise.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.520
You know, people say 10,000 steps,

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.930
that's also kind of overstated.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.300
Caffeine, 44 milligrams,
not really a problem.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.973
- So I committed to making
10 key lifestyle changes

00:01:08.973 --> 00:01:10.920
to see if I could turn this all around.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.410
- I'm curious what these 10
key lifestyle changes are

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.230
because so many people,
especially influencers fall

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.420
into fads that they think are healthy

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.200
but just result in short-term
goals being achieved.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.030
Like hitting a certain number on a scale.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.380
But hitting a certain number on a scale

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.820
with an unhealthy habit

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.010
is not something that's
good for your health.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.290
- The first five days were horrible.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.270
I dropped immediately from
three to four cups of tea

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.040
and coffee a day to zero.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.840
And while I did think
this would be challenging,

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.150
I had no idea that I'd
be practically unable

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.230
to function without it.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.460
- It's pretty interesting that even

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.830
with such a small amount
of caffeine in his diet,

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.390
he was already feeling
the effects of that.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:48.060
The common thing that we hear
is if you quit cold turkey

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.830
any kind of caffeine substance,

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.120
you start developing headaches.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.620
Usually we theorize this

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.470
is because the blood vessels
in your brain start to expand

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.690
'cause caffeine actually
constricts blood vessels.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.040
And when they're allowed to expand,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.030
when that happens in your head,

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.560
it creates a headache sensation.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.360
- And what made this
slightly harder was the fact

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.070
that at the same time my gym regimen

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.600
had just tripled in intensity.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.610
- Yeah, so if you're increasing activity

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.380
and at the same time decreasing caffeine,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.550
that's gonna be quite hard.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:15.120
Because remember what caffeine
does is it fights off fatigue

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.550
by blocking adenosine receptors.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.620
Throughout the day, you
form more adenosine,

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.470
as a result, you feel more
sleepy as the day goes on.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.850
Now, the way that you can clear this

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.460
outside of ingesting
substances like caffeine

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.550
is by taking naps or by
sleeping a good night's sleep.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.353
- I was running at every
possible opportunity

00:02:31.353 --> 00:02:33.780
literally until I could
not take another step.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:34.620
- That's a problem.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.420
When you start over training

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.850
when you haven't been training
for a long period of time,

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.577
that is gonna be extremely problematic

00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:43.530
'cause it's gonna raise your
risk of developing an injury.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.480
Once you get injured, you're
gonna stop working out

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.670
and it's gonna damage your
ability to reach your goals.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.670
In general, when you are sedentary
for long periods of time,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.830
your ligaments get weaker,
your muscles get weaker.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.990
And it's usually not the
big muscles that suffer,

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:58.167
so you feel okay, it's the
small stabilizing muscles

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:00.240
within your low back, your hips,

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.582
your knee, that really
give you that support

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.950
when you're taking an uneasy step

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.410
when you are fatigued,
when you aren't able to

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.660
oxygenate your body, 'cause
you're huffing and puffing.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.460
- Plus I was making myself do 25 minutes

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.516
of fast walking at an incline
every evening on top of that

00:03:14.516 --> 00:03:16.530
- Fast walking on an incline is great

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.450
because that essentially
puts your heart rate

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.420
in the blue zone like an
ideal fat burning zone.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.100
And it won't stress you out

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.220
so that you can continue doing
longer sessions like this.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.920
It's actually a great way
to build up an aerobic base.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:33.150
- The scales we're saying
83.8 kilos and 20.3% fat.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.040
- A lot of the weight
that you lose initially

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.450
usually happens to be water weight

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.100
when you start exercising quite heavily.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.300
Also it depends on what time

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.530
of the day you're weighing yourself.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.900
Ideally, this is right
after using the bathroom

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.810
in the morning, naked
because that allows you

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:46.980
to be the most consistent

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.170
- Over the next couple of
weeks, as all the other stuff,

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.940
I started to properly turn my attention

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.410
to the art of meditation.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.360
From everything I'd
heard about meditating,

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.070
I knew that this was gonna be the key

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.870
to reducing my overall stress levels.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.050
- Meditation, mindfulness
is extremely powerful.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.483
You don't have to sit cross-legged

00:04:02.483 --> 00:04:05.610
with your fingers touching in
order for it to be effective.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:08.610
There's multiple ways an
individual can be mindful,

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.800
be present in the moment or meditate.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.690
For some that means
sitting in a quiet room,

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.150
for others it could mean
people-watching at the coffee shop.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.550
It's really just about
being present in the moment

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.650
because a lot of times
our anxieties will take us

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.690
either to the future or to the past,

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.730
both places that we
don't have control over.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.930
So by being in the present

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.190
and understanding you have control

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.950
over the given moment
does reduce stress levels.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.370
We have seen this in good
quality scientific research.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.940
- But the other side to
this coin is the eating.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.561
At the point where I
decided to make this change,

00:04:36.561 --> 00:04:38.340
I was eating horribly.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.393
Eating junk food had
essentially become my way

00:04:40.393 --> 00:04:42.450
of pushing myself to work harder.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.000
- Eating junk food can become an addiction

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.430
like anything else that
is inherently rewarding

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.650
to the reward center of your brain.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.780
You eat junk food, dopamine gets released,

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.730
other feel good
neurotransmitters get released

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.560
and you keep doing it
when you're stressed.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.930
It's basically a form of self medication

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.060
but an unhealthy way of self medication.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.320
Just like how we have healthy

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.000
and unhealthy coping mechanisms.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.160
- This challenge really
forced me to get creative

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.060
with my recipes.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.680
I was really craving pancakes.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.669
Obviously I couldn't make
myself the full fat version

00:05:09.669 --> 00:05:11.370
but that allowed me to figure out

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.639
a recipe that was pretty lean, very quick,

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:16.106
and really tasty once
served with some blueberries

00:05:16.106 --> 00:05:17.190
and a bit of honey.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.010
- The idea is to create a
healthy relationship with foods

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:23.700
and to control and stop yourself
from eating out of control.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.280
And that will go a long
way to keeping you healthy.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.980
Everyone is going to
eat something unhealthy

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:29.820
every now and then.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.430
It's very hard for most people
to be perfect all the time.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.630
And it's not even something

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.400
that most doctors would recommend.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.100
Because in medicine seeking perfection

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.130
ultimately yields negative
outcomes in many cases

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.440
'cause the body is firmly placed

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.640
in a state of homeostasis,

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.830
which means balance not perfection.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.240
- By this point, I could actually feel

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.350
like I was in better shape.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:50.183
I felt lighter.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:51.150
I felt more agile.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.090
Not to mention that my weight
was now sitting at 81 kilos

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.650
which isn't even close
to actually factoring

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:58.380
in the full difference because
as well as losing the fat,

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.330
I was putting on muscle at the same time.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.090
It's even weird all these minor
stumbles I had with my diet.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.070
I think the fact that I wasn't too hard

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:06.840
on myself when I had to be a bit unhealthy

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.000
meant that I never felt
like it was all over

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.260
or what's the point anymore.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.321
- See this is a good
example of not being afraid

00:06:13.321 --> 00:06:15.870
of taking three steps
forward and one step back

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.812
and still seeing that
you're making progress

00:06:17.812 --> 00:06:20.520
because very often I see patients fall

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.740
into this cycle where they're doing well.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.510
They're trying to be
as perfect as possible,

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.130
then one thing goes wrong

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.780
because they're in a
place where they can't eat

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.460
or there was a temptation,
they can't eat healthy,

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.480
and there was a temptation.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.430
They say, "Oh, I need to punish myself.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:33.540
I need to feel shame.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:34.830
I need to feel remorse."

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.000
And then when they feel that way,

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.380
they want to eat more unhealthy foods

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.660
and then they go back
and fall into their cycle

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.560
of eating unhealthy.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.319
Whereas, if they take
the opposite approach,

00:06:42.319 --> 00:06:44.430
which Mrwhosetheboss here took

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:46.740
and say, "Okay, but I'm
still two steps ahead

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.480
so I can continue on this
journey and keep crushing it.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:49.800
Even if I took three steps back,

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.780
I'm still ahead from
where I was last week,

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.010
so I'm gonna keep pushing on."

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.420
That's where you get the best outcomes.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:56.160
It's like really having the stamina

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.500
to keep going forward and stay motivated.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.870
- Three months ago, I got
myself this standing desk

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.630
and I spent an average of
four hours per day working

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:04.463
from it.

00:07:04.463 --> 00:07:05.880
I could not recommend it more.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.170
Because it's not just that you stand

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.430
and you keep your core active,

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:10.230
but you also find that
you move your legs more

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.600
your arms more, and you're
just generally active

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:15.300
for four more hours a
day, which is enormous.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.770
And this board that I've been using-

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.360
- Spoiler alert for everyone
watching this video. (laughs)

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:23.580
I have the same thing underneath my desk

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:27.090
and I don't use it just
under my standing desk here

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:27.923
while I'm standing,

00:07:27.923 --> 00:07:29.130
but also while I'm sitting right now.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.960
It actually allows me
to keep my feet busy.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.660
And studies have shown that
those who like tap their feet

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.180
and especially when you have
something fidgety like this

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.100
actually burn more calories
throughout the day,

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.780
so I'm with this type of advice here.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:40.613
- And then every now and again

00:07:40.613 --> 00:07:42.600
I've been swapping it out
for this vibration plate

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.940
which basically exercises my body for me.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.140
- Okay, I don't know.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:48.750
Quick fixes, gimmicks,
cool If you enjoy them,

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:50.400
not mandatory by any means

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.530
- Like one thing I used
was Slendertone belt

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.730
that shocks your abs

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.070
into contracting many times very quickly.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:58.290
- This is where like
we get into the hacks,

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.370
the gimmicky stuff.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.350
This is the stuff that I
think most people do not need.

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:03.930
And I think hyper optimization
and hyper focusing

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:06.720
on these results will
actually yield worse outcomes

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:07.553
in the long term.

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.120
Because my job as a
doctor is not to give you

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.860
the best transformation in a hundred days,

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.960
but to help you live a
hundred healthy years

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.580
because I could easily strap on a bunch

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:15.900
of these things and make your quality

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.220
of life absolutely terrible

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.380
and drive up your anxiety so high.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:20.550
All the potential benefits

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.710
of these gadgets end up backfiring.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:23.910
- One of my other resolutions

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.590
was to install a water reminder app

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:26.423
on my phone that pings me every two hours

00:08:26.423 --> 00:08:28.530
to make sure I drink.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.390
- I think this is another gimmicky thing.

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:32.430
The majority of people don't
need a reminder like this

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:33.450
because what ends up happening,

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.710
and I could tell you this as a physician

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.350
with many years of practice,
you develop alarm fatigue

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.000
where you get so many notifications

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.650
especially ones that aren't super urgent

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:42.930
like this one that you
end up ignoring it once,

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:45.120
twice three times, and then
you forget all about it.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.830
Its value becomes meaningless to you.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:47.850
- I thought this was genius.

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:48.960
I thought this was gonna solve

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.370
my hydration problems forever.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:51.810
- What hydration problem is he having?

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:54.060
I'm curious, because
carrying a water bottle

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:56.490
with you will inherently
remind you to drink

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.440
and that you probably
don't need a reminder

00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.273
on your phone for that.

00:08:59.273 --> 00:09:00.870
- It did gimme a nudge at the beginning,

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.353
but by the time we were
approaching week 10,

00:09:03.353 --> 00:09:05.520
the regularity of it almost made me start

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.353
to just tune out the notification.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.100
- It's like we know
what we're talking about

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:11.933
in healthcare.

00:09:11.933 --> 00:09:13.260
- That said, the biggest thing

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.820
that was actually a game changer

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.890
was just making sure that
I always had a full bottle.

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:18.210
- Bro, this hilarious.

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:19.043
It's like...

00:09:19.043 --> 00:09:20.085
No, that can't be.

00:09:20.085 --> 00:09:21.412
And this is my first time watching.

