00:09:22.391 --> 00:09:23.224
(Dr. Mike laughing)

00:09:23.224 --> 00:09:26.400
- This made me feel less
hungry and even more awake.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.170
- And he's right here in saying that

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.030
because when you start developing mild

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.200
to moderate dehydration,

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.970
your metabolism does start to suffer.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:35.010
So keeping it in a healthy range,

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.570
which again doesn't take a lot of work,

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.250
doesn't take a meticulous tracking,

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:40.800
will help you get to and
stay at a healthy weight.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.630
- It was at around day 75,

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.040
three quarters through the challenge,

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.300
where I actually started to notice

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:47.040
that I was also getting much stronger.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.590
I was lifting about 80%
more than when I started.

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:51.664
- Yeah the biggest joy that
people get from weightlifting

00:09:51.664 --> 00:09:53.640
is seeing that progress.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.410
No matter if you lift lightweights

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:58.770
for higher reps or heavy
weights for lower reps,

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:00.420
you're gonna see progress go up.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.640
The most important thing when
it comes to weight lifting

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.770
in order to see
improvements is consistency

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.030
and injury prevention.

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:08.430
I cannot tell you how many people stop

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:11.100
their weight training
journeys because of injuries

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.650
usually due to incorrect
form or ego lifting

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:14.883
which is when you put too much weight on

00:10:14.883 --> 00:10:18.210
that your incapable of handling
and end up hurting yourself.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:20.400
- Not to mention that while
at the start I was planking

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:21.840
for about a minute a go,

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.480
by this point I was becoming
able to do three minute planks.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:25.313
- That's really good,

00:10:25.313 --> 00:10:27.060
I can't do a three minute
plank, shout out to him.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.890
- By the time we got today 85,

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.720
my sleep was drastically better

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.570
than the 28% I was being scored
when I started this change.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.630
I was now regularly hitting
70 to 80% sleep quality

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.430
which was already a vast improvement.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:40.524
- If you sleep the
consistent number of hours

00:10:40.524 --> 00:10:43.500
of sleep per night at the same time of day

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.170
and you're sleeping eight
hours a night, 11:00 to 7:00,

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:47.157
and you keep doing that every night,

00:10:47.157 --> 00:10:48.930
11:00 to 7:00, 11:00
to 7:00, 11:00 to 7:00,

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.660
and you feel good and you
don't have daytime somnolence

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:52.980
where you feel like you're sleepy,

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.020
you're not waking up feeling exhausted,

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:57.510
you don't need things to
tell you your sleep quality.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.470
'Cause here's the problem,

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.060
we've actually done research with this.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.920
We've told certain participants

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.600
even after they had a good night's sleep

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.220
that their quality of sleep was bad.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.390
And we compared them with people

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.070
whose sleep quality was actually bad

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:09.330
and we told them that it was good.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:11.490
And the outcomes of how they performed

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:13.140
actually ended up almost switching

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:15.450
because these individuals were so affected

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.310
by the numbers they saw in apps like this

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:19.740
that it didn't even matter that
they got good quality sleep.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.236
So I I'm really hesitant
to use apps like this

00:11:22.236 --> 00:11:25.020
that aren't carefully
clinically monitored.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:27.120
And I see so many glitches in these apps

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:30.000
that I don't want them guiding
my patients in general.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.833
Now, if you're enjoying it

00:11:30.833 --> 00:11:32.850
and it's something you
do for fun, that's fine

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:35.400
but be careful making health
decisions off apps like this.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.510
- But then I found this product,

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:38.130
it's an air filtration unit

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.320
that actually just sucks
in all the allergens,

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:41.264
the dust and the pollen

00:11:41.264 --> 00:11:43.470
that have been restricting
my breathing at night.

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.330
- Okay, so those particles
are not necessarily

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.350
restricting his breathing.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:49.140
What happens when you get
an air purifier like that

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.430
usually with a HEPA filter,

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.340
it clears out the allergens
that cause your body

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.920
to have an allergic
reaction within your airways

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:58.560
leading them to swell and block airflow

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.630
or create a constriction in the airflow.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.670
As a result, it feels
like you can't breathe.

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:05.430
But it's not actually the
particles blocking you up

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:06.780
as if it's a plumbing system.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.580
And I would actually recommend that people

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.370
with allergies or people
who end up mouth breathing

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.200
get a humidifier in the room as well.

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:15.960
It allows you for your mucus
membranes to stay moist.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:16.793
When they're moist,

00:12:16.793 --> 00:12:18.270
you're more likely to
be comfortable sleeping

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:20.790
throughout the night and not
wake up from a dry mouth.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.790
And also it prevents cracking
of those mucus membranes

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.170
which can lead to infections.

